WEBVTT

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.090
Over the past ten years or more,

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:06.594
I worked closely together with the late,

00:05:06.635 --> 00:05:10.681
great anthropologist David Graeber

00:05:10.681 --> 00:05:13.476
to address some of these questions.

00:05:13.517 --> 00:05:15.353
But we did it on a much larger scale

00:05:15.353 --> 00:05:20.524
because from our perspective
as an archaeologist and an anthropologist,

00:05:20.566 --> 00:05:24.236
this clash between theory and data,

00:05:24.278 --> 00:05:26.864
between the standard narrative
of human history

00:05:26.864 --> 00:05:29.909
and the evidence
that we have before us today

00:05:29.909 --> 00:05:33.120
is not just confined
to the early Middle East.